# Miquel's pivot theorem — circles AEF, BFD, CDE through points D, E, F on the sides of a triangle share a common point (source: Miquel; Johnson, Advanced Euclidean Geometry)
A B C = triangle
D = on_line(B, C)
E = on_line(C, A)
F = on_line(A, B)
M = meet(circumcircle(A, E, F), circumcircle(B, F, D))
prove cyclic(C, D, E, M)
